WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:04.033
-House Republicans defied
Donald Trump on a secret ballot

00:00:04.033 --> 00:00:05.701
to choose their nominee for
the next Speaker of the House.

00:00:05.701 --> 00:00:07.601
But the chamber is still
completely paralyzed

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:09.734
as Republicans scramble
to get the votes together

00:00:09.734 --> 00:00:13.234
in a process that has been both
very chaotic and very weird.

00:00:13.234 --> 00:00:15.734
For more on this, it's time
for "A Closer Look."

00:00:15.734 --> 00:00:18.300
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:19.734 --> 00:00:21.734
As we have said many times
on this show,

00:00:21.734 --> 00:00:24.234
Donald Trump weirdified
the Republican Party.

00:00:24.234 --> 00:00:26.434
They were always weird,
but for the most part,

00:00:26.434 --> 00:00:28.534
they had enough shame
to keep their weirdness hidden.

00:00:28.534 --> 00:00:30.234
But then Trump came along
and unleashed

00:00:30.234 --> 00:00:34.467
an army of mutant freaks like
Mike Lindell or Rudy Giuliani,

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:38.400
seen here attempting
to hypnotize you into forgetting

00:00:38.400 --> 00:00:40.767
that he is wearing
a pair of child's khakis

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:42.133
as his golf shorts.

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:43.934
[As Giuliani]
You're getting very sleepy.

00:00:43.934 --> 00:00:47.100
But wait! That's me!

00:00:47.100 --> 00:00:48.601
I'm getting very sleepy.

00:00:48.601 --> 00:00:52.100
Must have been
my breakfast whiskey.

00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:55.634
It doesn't make the Cheerios
soggy like milk does.

00:00:55.634 --> 00:00:57.501
[Normal voice]
There was no reason

00:00:57.501 --> 00:01:00.901
to show you that video today.

00:01:00.901 --> 00:01:02.767
None at all.

00:01:02.767 --> 00:01:06.100
But it's the best.
So why not?

00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:07.968
There was a point.

00:01:07.968 --> 00:01:10.968
Oh, yeah!
Donald Trump...is weird.

00:01:10.968 --> 00:01:13.634
For example, he's a big fan
of Ohio Congressman Jim Jordan,

00:01:13.634 --> 00:01:15.434
who Trump recently endorsed
for Speaker of the House.

00:01:15.434 --> 00:01:19.133
In the past, Trump has praised
Jordan for the weirdest reasons.

00:01:19.133 --> 00:01:21.467
For example, Jordan rarely
wears a suit jacket,

00:01:21.467 --> 00:01:23.100
and Trump noticed that

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.133
and took away the weirdest
possible interpretation.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:31.434
-When I first got to know Jim,
I said, "Huh!

00:01:31.434 --> 00:01:35.267
He never wears a jacket.
What the hell's going on?

00:01:35.267 --> 00:01:37.767
He's obviously very proud
of his body."

00:01:37.767 --> 00:01:40.167
[ Laughter ]

00:01:42.601 --> 00:01:44.934
-Well, I guess we know
how Trump feels about his body.

00:01:44.934 --> 00:01:47.734
If his jackets
were any bigger,

00:01:47.734 --> 00:01:50.968
they would technically
be cocoons.

00:01:50.968 --> 00:01:52.467
And again, I know
everybody stopped

00:01:52.467 --> 00:01:53.868
caring about hypocrisy
years ago,

00:01:53.868 --> 00:01:55.834
but just imagine
how conservatives would react

00:01:55.834 --> 00:01:57.334
if Joe Biden was out
on the stump

00:01:57.334 --> 00:01:58.868
talking about
the body positivity

00:01:58.868 --> 00:02:00.567
of the men
in the Democratic Party.

00:02:00.567 --> 00:02:01.968
"I'll tell you,
our caucus right now

00:02:01.968 --> 00:02:05.634
is just one Gosling
after the other."

00:02:05.634 --> 00:02:07.667
Now, as I mentioned,
Trump endorsed Jim Jordan

00:02:07.667 --> 00:02:09.033
to be the next
Speaker of the House.

00:02:09.033 --> 00:02:11.234
Jordan ran against Louisiana
Congressman Steve Scalise

00:02:11.234 --> 00:02:12.567
for the GOP nomination,

00:02:12.567 --> 00:02:15.234
and the conference voted
on Wednesday in a secret ballot.

00:02:15.234 --> 00:02:16.567
In fact, the ballot
was so secret,

00:02:16.567 --> 00:02:18.234
they made everyone
put their phones

00:02:18.234 --> 00:02:20.434
in manila envelopes
before entering the room.

00:02:20.434 --> 00:02:22.701
Unfortunately, Republicans
accidentally put stamps

00:02:22.701 --> 00:02:25.968
on all those envelopes and their
phones got mailed to the FBI.

00:02:25.968 --> 00:02:28.868
"Boss, you're not
gonna believe this,

00:02:28.868 --> 00:02:30.200
but we just cracked the case."

00:02:30.200 --> 00:02:31.200
"Which one?"

00:02:31.200 --> 00:02:32.834
"All of them!"

00:02:32.834 --> 00:02:34.200
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.200 --> 00:02:36.934
So, Trump endorsed Jim Jordan,
and Trump proudly touts

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.434
his control
over the Republican Party,

00:02:38.434 --> 00:02:40.434
claiming the people
he endorses always win.

00:02:40.434 --> 00:02:42.667
So Jordan must have
cruised to victory, right?

00:02:42.667 --> 00:02:44.000
Back me up, clip!

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:45.000
-We have breaking news.

00:02:45.000 --> 00:02:46.634
House Republicans have nominated

00:02:46.634 --> 00:02:48.601
Steve Scalise moments ago

00:02:48.601 --> 00:02:49.968
as their new speaker.

00:02:49.968 --> 00:02:52.200
-Trump endorsed Jordan,
you know,

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:54.434
more than maybe
about a week ago.

00:02:54.434 --> 00:02:57.801
So a big loss
for Trump here, as well.

00:02:57.801 --> 00:02:59.767
-Ooh, Trump's not gonna
be happy about that.

00:02:59.767 --> 00:03:01.834
[As Trump] Steve Scalise
is a loser and a nobody.

00:03:01.834 --> 00:03:05.000
And on top of that,
he wears a jacket.

00:03:05.000 --> 00:03:07.067
Unlike Jim Jordan,
who has a terrific body.

00:03:07.067 --> 00:03:09.601
You know, I always thought
members of Congress should

00:03:09.601 --> 00:03:11.100
dress like Chippendale dancers.

00:03:11.100 --> 00:03:12.601
Chippendales.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.334
We love Chippendales, don't we?

00:03:14.334 --> 00:03:18.267
You know, for a long time,
I thought it was Chip and Dale,

00:03:18.267 --> 00:03:20.434
and I was very surprised
that bachelorettes wanted

00:03:20.434 --> 00:03:22.901
to go to a place where chipmunks
would give them lap dances,

00:03:22.901 --> 00:03:26.133
because they may look cute,
but they're filthy animals.

00:03:26.133 --> 00:03:27.434
They're filthy.

00:03:27.434 --> 00:03:29.767
You don't want them
near your lap.

00:03:29.767 --> 00:03:32.767
They're just rats
with nicer coats.

00:03:32.767 --> 00:03:34.968
[Normal voice] So, Steve Scalise
is now technically

00:03:34.968 --> 00:03:36.901
the GOP's nominee for speaker,
but that doesn't mean

00:03:36.901 --> 00:03:38.601
he has enough votes
to actually become speaker.

00:03:38.601 --> 00:03:41.334
Once the full House
goes to the floor to vote,

00:03:41.334 --> 00:03:43.601
he has to keep making promises
to people to get their votes,

00:03:43.601 --> 00:03:45.767
just like now former speaker
Kevin McCarthy did.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.367
The situation
has been so chaotic,

00:03:47.367 --> 00:03:49.300
reporters are just grabbing
members of Congress

00:03:49.300 --> 00:03:51.000
in the halls at random,

00:03:51.000 --> 00:03:53.467
live on camera, to ask them
who they're voting for.

00:03:53.467 --> 00:03:55.367
-As we watch one of
the defectors walk by now,

00:03:55.367 --> 00:03:59.033
one of the people who ousted
Kevin McCarthy, Tim Burchett.

00:03:59.033 --> 00:04:01.868
Mr. Burchett, you gonna vote
for Mr. Scalise on the floor?

00:04:01.868 --> 00:04:03.467
-Absolutely.
-Thank you, Congressman.

00:04:03.467 --> 00:04:06.133
He's on board -- Steve Scalise.
There's some news just now.

00:04:06.133 --> 00:04:10.133
He is gonna be on the Scalise
board, the Scalise train.

00:04:10.133 --> 00:04:13.601
But there are others at this
moment who have yet to commit.

00:04:13.601 --> 00:04:14.934
-That's how much of a mess

00:04:14.934 --> 00:04:16.534
Republicans have made
of this situation.

00:04:16.534 --> 00:04:18.400
They've turned
professional reporters into guys

00:04:18.400 --> 00:04:21.701
handing out fliers for
comedy shows in Times Square.

00:04:21.701 --> 00:04:23.834
"Hey, you want to come see
some comedy? It's free."

00:04:23.834 --> 00:04:25.467
By the way,
what kind of crappy comic

00:04:25.467 --> 00:04:28.200
would need to hand out fliers
for a show in Times Square?

00:04:28.200 --> 00:04:31.200
Oh, son of a bitch!

00:04:31.200 --> 00:04:33.000
So, the GOP infighting
has been a mess.

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:35.467
It's also been, as we mentioned
before, incredibly weird.

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:38.701
For example, Wyoming
Congressman Harriet Hageman

00:04:38.701 --> 00:04:42.267
showed up to GOP forum
on Tuesday holding a lasso.

00:04:42.267 --> 00:04:46.534
Is she gonna vote for a speaker
or try to catch one?

00:04:46.534 --> 00:04:48.534
That's how [bleep] the job
of Republican speaker is --

00:04:48.534 --> 00:04:51.968
they've got to hog-tie you down
just to make you take it.

00:04:51.968 --> 00:04:54.100
Is this a meeting to elect
a new Speaker of the House

00:04:54.100 --> 00:04:55.334
or a county fair?

00:04:55.334 --> 00:04:56.667
After they choose a speaker,

00:04:56.667 --> 00:04:59.834
are they also gonna judge
who has the biggest pumpkin?

00:04:59.834 --> 00:05:01.534
Which brings us
to a segment called

00:05:01.534 --> 00:05:03.701
"We Could Have Made
a Trump Joke Here."

00:05:03.701 --> 00:05:05.834
[ Laughter ]

00:05:08.334 --> 00:05:12.634
Are they also gonna judge
who has the biggest pumpkin?

00:05:12.634 --> 00:05:16.133
And then we're just
gonna let it go.

00:05:16.133 --> 00:05:19.300
We're better than that.

00:05:19.300 --> 00:05:21.801
We've moved on
from that kind of joke.

00:05:21.801 --> 00:05:24.634
[ Laughter ]

00:05:24.634 --> 00:05:26.200
I mean, if we were gonna
make a joke

00:05:26.200 --> 00:05:29.200
about the biggest pumpkin
in the GOP, you know,

00:05:29.200 --> 00:05:30.934
we'd show you this picture.

00:05:30.934 --> 00:05:32.767
[ Laughter ]

00:05:32.767 --> 00:05:34.501
Now, that's a photo
we're never gonna retire,

00:05:34.501 --> 00:05:36.133
especially now that
it's Halloween season.

00:05:36.133 --> 00:05:38.067
Imagine that thing
sitting on the porch

00:05:38.067 --> 00:05:39.400
waiting for trick-or-treaters.

00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.968
Wouldn't you want to see
what it would look like

00:05:40.968 --> 00:05:42.467
if Rudy was
one of those paintings

00:05:42.467 --> 00:05:44.067
whose eyes followed you
around the room?

00:05:44.067 --> 00:05:46.067
Well, here you go.

00:05:46.067 --> 00:05:48.901
[ Laughter ]

00:05:51.100 --> 00:05:53.934
But, of course, a lasso was not
the weirdest fashion choice

00:05:53.934 --> 00:05:56.234
at the GOP conference this week.
As we mentioned yesterday,

00:05:56.234 --> 00:05:58.467
South Carolina
Congresswoman Nancy Mace

00:05:58.467 --> 00:06:01.601
showed up wearing a shirt
with the letter "A,"

00:06:01.601 --> 00:06:03.300
which she said
was a scarlet letter

00:06:03.300 --> 00:06:05.067
because she voted
to oust former speaker

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:07.534
Kevin McCarthy last week
and got criticized for it.

00:06:07.534 --> 00:06:09.801
-I'm wearing the scarlet letter
after the week

00:06:09.801 --> 00:06:12.634
that I just had last week,
being a woman up here

00:06:12.634 --> 00:06:15.801
and being demonized for my vote
and for my voice.

00:06:15.801 --> 00:06:17.934
-Okay, but that doesn't look
like the scarlet letter.

00:06:17.934 --> 00:06:19.734
That looked like you stole
the last letter

00:06:19.734 --> 00:06:21.834
of the Chick-fil-A logo.

00:06:21.834 --> 00:06:23.534
[ Laughter ]

00:06:23.534 --> 00:06:25.067
Mace is one of the holdouts

00:06:25.067 --> 00:06:27.367
threatening to tank
Scalise's speakership bid.

00:06:27.367 --> 00:06:29.100
She told CNN's Jake Tapper
yesterday

00:06:29.100 --> 00:06:31.634
that she would vote for Jordan
when it got to the floor.

00:06:31.634 --> 00:06:34.234
And she even claimed
there were some Democrats --

00:06:34.234 --> 00:06:36.834
not Republicans, Democrats --
who said they could trust

00:06:36.834 --> 00:06:39.501
Jordan, one of the most
pro-MAGA members of Congress,

00:06:39.501 --> 00:06:41.834
who helped instigate
the January 6th coup.

00:06:41.834 --> 00:06:45.267
And her claim left Tapper
in stunned disbelief.

00:06:45.267 --> 00:06:47.367
-Well, I think Jim Jordan
is not out of the mix.

00:06:47.367 --> 00:06:49.200
I've talked to a lot of people
who still support him.

00:06:49.200 --> 00:06:50.734
I've actually
talked to Democrats

00:06:50.734 --> 00:06:52.467
who trust him at his word.

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:54.300
I don't think that's out
of the realm of possibility --

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:56.767
-Jim Jordan?
-Yes, I've talked to Democrats

00:06:56.767 --> 00:06:58.534
over the last week
on who do they trust,

00:06:58.534 --> 00:07:00.934
even though they wouldn't agree
with him on many issues.

00:07:00.934 --> 00:07:02.567
He is someone --
-The Jim Jordan from Ohio?

00:07:02.567 --> 00:07:04.234
-Oh, yes, the Jim Jordan
from Ohio. I talk to people --

00:07:04.234 --> 00:07:05.701
-Democrats in Congress?

00:07:05.701 --> 00:07:07.601
-Yes, they can work with him,
and those that I have --

00:07:07.601 --> 00:07:09.567
-Name one Democrat from Congress
that trusts Jim Jordan.

00:07:09.567 --> 00:07:11.734
-I'm not gonna name people
off the record.

00:07:11.734 --> 00:07:14.567
They trust him more than
they trust the former speaker,

00:07:14.567 --> 00:07:17.067
in my private conversations
with Democrats.

00:07:17.067 --> 00:07:21.234
-The worse Republicans get,
the sassier Tapper gets.

00:07:21.234 --> 00:07:25.567
"The Jim Jordan from Ohio?

00:07:25.567 --> 00:07:28.067
With the rockin' bod?"

00:07:28.067 --> 00:07:30.501
[ Laughter ]

00:07:30.501 --> 00:07:33.000
We said it yesterday,
and we'll say it again today.

00:07:33.000 --> 00:07:36.033
Republican Party,
you just got tapped.

00:07:37.067 --> 00:07:38.567
[ Air horn blasting ]

00:07:38.567 --> 00:07:41.734
[ Guitar solo ]

00:07:41.734 --> 00:07:44.067
[ Man screams ]

00:07:44.067 --> 00:07:45.734
[ Laughter ]

00:07:49.367 --> 00:07:51.400
But regardless of who wins
the speaker vote,

00:07:51.400 --> 00:07:53.467
they're both extremists,
they both voted to overturn

00:07:53.467 --> 00:07:55.100
the 2020 election
on January 6th,

00:07:55.100 --> 00:07:56.434
and neither will acknowledge

00:07:56.434 --> 00:07:58.033
that Joe Biden was
the legitimate winner,

00:07:58.033 --> 00:08:00.434
which led Colorado
Congressman Ken Buck to say

00:08:00.434 --> 00:08:01.901
he couldn't vote
for either of them.

00:08:01.901 --> 00:08:03.434
-I asked last night,

00:08:03.434 --> 00:08:06.033
"Will you unequivocally
and publicly state

00:08:06.033 --> 00:08:08.400
that the election,
the 2020 presidential election,

00:08:08.400 --> 00:08:09.968
was not stolen?"

00:08:09.968 --> 00:08:12.133
He didn't answer
that question very clearly,

00:08:12.133 --> 00:08:14.634
and Jim Jordan didn't answer
that question very clearly.

00:08:14.634 --> 00:08:17.501
-Something as simple as saying
the 2020 election wasn't stolen,

00:08:17.501 --> 00:08:19.868
why don't you think either
one of those gentlemen

00:08:19.868 --> 00:08:21.467
can commit to that?

00:08:21.467 --> 00:08:24.601
-I think there is a large group
of Trump followers

00:08:24.601 --> 00:08:27.667
in this country
that would disagree with that,

00:08:27.667 --> 00:08:30.601
and would -- there would be
a political penalty

00:08:30.601 --> 00:08:32.100
for saying such a thing.

00:08:32.100 --> 00:08:33.367
-Yeah, Republicans
are so desperate

00:08:33.367 --> 00:08:34.434
to please the Trump base,

00:08:34.434 --> 00:08:36.167
they're doing
increasingly dumb [bleep]

00:08:36.167 --> 00:08:37.834
bringing, like, a lasso
to a meeting

00:08:37.834 --> 00:08:40.234
or dressing like an off-brand
Captain America

00:08:40.234 --> 00:08:43.067
your grandma would get
at a dollar store.

00:08:43.067 --> 00:08:45.634
"The man at the store said
this one is just as good!

00:08:45.634 --> 00:08:48.567
You just can't eat the paint
or leave it out in the sun.

00:08:48.567 --> 00:08:51.133
She was right next to
discount Wonder Woman."

00:08:51.133 --> 00:08:53.033
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:54.868
But that explains
everything right there.

00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:56.534
Republicans are terrified
of the Trump base

00:08:56.534 --> 00:08:58.767
and pro-Trump media, even though
it does not represent

00:08:58.767 --> 00:09:01.000
and has never represented
a majority of Americans.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:02.334
It hasn't even come close.

00:09:02.334 --> 00:09:04.400
But it's a big enough part
of the GOP base

00:09:04.400 --> 00:09:06.000
to make Republican
politicians afraid,

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:08.234
which is why
they could only vote

00:09:08.234 --> 00:09:11.167
against Trump's pick for speaker
when it was a secret ballot,

00:09:11.167 --> 00:09:12.467
because they all know
the truth --

00:09:12.467 --> 00:09:14.133
Trump is a dangerous
aspiring dictator

00:09:14.133 --> 00:09:16.067
who wants to dismantle
American democracy,

00:09:16.067 --> 00:09:17.400
and who looks like a pumpkin!

00:09:17.400 --> 00:09:20.334
Alright, fine, we said it!
Sue me!

00:09:20.334 --> 00:09:23.267
We had one Trump pumpkin.
We've been waiting hard.

00:09:23.267 --> 00:09:24.701
You know what?
We've worked hard.

00:09:24.701 --> 00:09:26.067
We've worked two weeks
in a row.

00:09:26.067 --> 00:09:28.467
Yeah, I know we had
five months off before that,

00:09:28.467 --> 00:09:29.934
but that's two weeks
in a row.

00:09:29.934 --> 00:09:32.334
Name one other American
who's done that.

00:09:32.334 --> 00:09:35.000
[ Laughter ]

00:09:35.000 --> 00:09:36.801
When they write the book
on me one day,

00:09:36.801 --> 00:09:38.167
I just hope they say
that Seth Meyers

00:09:38.167 --> 00:09:40.000
wasn't proud of that joke,
but he is...

00:09:40.000 --> 00:09:41.834
-Very proud of his body.

00:09:41.834 --> 00:09:43.834
[ Laughter ]

00:09:43.834 --> 00:09:46.834
-No jacket, baby! No jacket!

00:09:46.834 --> 00:09:49.167
[ Laughing ]
This has been "A Closer Look."

00:09:49.167 --> 00:09:51.801
[ Cheers and applause ]

